Q1. In-scope ids read as fixed on the trigger as written: F15-1 `env.rs:300`, F14-1 `env.rs:198`, F15-2/F14-2 `models.rs` cap keeps seated pairs, F15-3 `smoke.rs:303`, F14-3 `smoke.rs:383`, F14-4 `smoke.rs:300`, F14-5 ten-minute rule, F15-5 re-read after rollback, F15-6 switch-before-lock, F16-1/F17-5 `web.rs:83,188`; --rev/--diff: F19-1/F20-1 `http.rs:1271`, F19-2/F18-4/F20-6 redactor+ignore, F19-3/F20-3 `<stem>.<sha8>` exclusive, F18-1/F19-6 `reviewed_info`+withheld, F18-2/F20-2 `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, F18-3 snapshot-after-patch, F18-5 `reviewed.rs:348`, F18-6 unlink-outside, F20-4 `--ignored`, F18-7 claim-after-staging, F19-5 shared check plus `--end-of-options`. F19-4/F20-5 were prior-commit items; nothing here contradicts them.

Q2. Legitimate refusals possible: CDN host with mixed public/private answers refuses the whole fetch; IPv6 or proxy deployments need review (finding #1); a revision spelled with trailing whitespace is trimmed and accepted. Hostile bypass of the direct trigger is closed at lookup and peer per hop; proxy and DNS-to-connect rebinding remain (finding #1); rev/diff syntax is checked before git in CLI and MCP.

Q3. Lookup thread past the deadline is left running (finding #1). Patch temp/hard-link, scratch dir (`Drop` removes only created dirs), worktree and lock handling otherwise read as cleaned up; no contrary path was read.

Q4. Non---rev runs keep the live-tree path, index connection and ledger keys; live HEAD has no `live_head` extra and priors are listed. Older host-keyed state is read without error and untrusted until re-fetched. `telemetry_parity` expectations were updated to URL keys. HTTP without patch is unchanged apart from extras plumbing.

Q5. Redaction keeps sha256 of the file as written and records a count, so the ledger matches what the reviewer saw; a missed secret shape would still leak, and an over-broad shape would mangle the diff — shapes were not exhaustively audited here. Withheld rule fires only for `--rev` whose sha differs from HEAD at plan time (finding #3).

Q6. Untested or thinly covered: real-network proxy behavior, stalled-lookup thread lifetime, link swap between kind-check and read, HEAD moving between plan and staging, patch budget refusal end-to-end over HTTP, and secret-shape recall/precision on patches.

### Findings

- **F29-1** [major] `crates/c3/src/maintain/env.rs:155` - Public-fetch origin check can be bypassed through a configured HTTP(S) proxy, and a stalled DNS lookup thread is left running past the 15 s deadline. Trigger: C3_MAINTAIN_TEST_HTTP off, real network with HTTPS_PROXY set and a public catalog hostname resolving to a private address; or a catalog hop whose lookup stalls past 15 s. Evidence: read-code: hop_agent builds a ureq agent with custom resolver and timeout_connect(remaining); SystemEnv::http_get does not clear proxy env and check_peer validates resp.remote_addr(), which under a proxy is the proxy peer, not the origin.; read-code: resolve_within spawns c3-maintain-dns thread and on recv_timeout returns Timeout while sender thread keeps running detached; fetch maps only post-deadline errors to the deadline text.; read-code: fetch re-validates start and each redirect hop as https without userinfo and requires a named public host plus a public peer at every hop. Verify: Run a public catalog fetch with a stub proxy and a private origin, record the peer that check_peer saw, and list threads after a stalled-lookup fetch. Remedy: Bypass or clear proxy env for public_only GETs (or resolve and dial without proxy), document proxy behavior, and detach/join the DNS thread with a bounded lifetime or a cached token so no thread outlives the deadline.
- **F29-2** [minor] `crates/c3/src/consult/reviewed.rs:348` - Staging link refusal has a check-to-read window: source_kind uses symlink_metadata plus canonicalize, but the brief/handoffs bytes are read later, so a link swapped in between is still read through. Trigger: A path that is a real dir/file at source_kind time is replaced by a symlink to outside the repo before stage_dir/stage_file reads it. Evidence: read-code: source_kind returns Linked for reparse points or canonical paths escaping the repo, else Dir/File; setup_review_tree then calls stage_dir/stage_file and brief_bytes in later statements with no re-check.; read-code: Doc promises nothing is ever read through a link, with linked handoffs/state counted in links_skipped. Verify: Interleave a link swap between the kind check and the copy in a fixture and confirm nothing outside the repo reaches the worktree. Remedy: Open staging sources with no-follow semantics (openat NOFOLLOW / symlink_metadata re-check at open) or re-validate symlink_metadata immediately before each read/copy and fail closed on change.
- **F29-3** [minor] `crates/c3/src/consult/orchestrate/mod.rs:1849` - Withheld-findings gating compares the planned --rev sha string with a fresh HEAD resolve at plan time; a HEAD that moves between resolve and staging, or an unresolvable HEAD, can withhold on live HEAD or list priors on another revision. Trigger: Concurrent commit moves HEAD after the plan-time resolve, or HEAD is unresolvable while --rev names the same logical tip. Evidence: read-code: priors_withheld is set when isolation is_rev and sha != resolve_commit(HEAD), then open_findings are cleared; reviewed_info/live_head come from the worktree fingerprint and pre-run revision_info.; read-code: Prompt shows one withheld sentence and asks for empty prior_findings; finish ignores the reply priors section when withheld. Verify: Move HEAD between plan and staging in a fixture and check whether priors are listed or withheld versus the revision actually read. Remedy: Decide withholding from the staged worktree sha versus the live HEAD read at the same post-staging point, and define the empty-HEAD behavior explicitly.

